  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Royal ceremonial ensemble of the Malay sultanates, held as regalia and played only for coronations, installations and other court rites; it survives in Kedah, Terengganu, Perak and Selangor and in Brunei. The core ensemble is the nehara kettledrum (a Persian-Indian naqareh card stands in), a pair of gendang nobat barrel drums, the serunai shawm and the long silver nafiri trumpet, with a gong in the Kedah ensemble.",
